ism for that to happen so we need  an amendment  to give congress the authority to do  that i believe i don't think they could  just change their own rules to do that  so that's what needs to happen  but let me tell you something else the  most important thing  that needs to happen and this is the  final thing i want to talk about on  today's show  today's main show  and that is  that i think this january 6 select  committee the riot committee whatever  you want to call it  they're now in over their heads  i do not think this committee  as it is right now  should be the lead investig  investigatory body  into the capitol riot  i believe that it is time for merrick  garland to finally step up  and appoint a special prosecutor  to officially start a criminal  investigation  into these events  now don't get me wrong  so far for the most part i have been  very happy with what the select  committee has done  and the reason i say they're in over  their heads  is because of the sheer scope  of what it is they're trying to do  which to be honest we don't even really  know everything they're attempting to do  yet  so you know we have to contend with that  you know they've got trump out there  they say oh we may be looking at  criminal activity here we may be looking  at criminal activity with these  individuals we got roger stone we got  steve bannon now we got members of  congress  and they can't  even if they're from opposing parties  heck almost especially if they're from  opposing parties  they now really can't  do this in a non-partisan way  because you do have lawmakers that do  have to answer these questions they  absolutely have to  that's why a special prosecutor is now  needed convene a grand jury  and essentially take it over for the  most part  because  the optics are always going to be bad  if you have a democrat-controlled  committee  subpoenaing republican members of  congress republicans are going to  weaponize that to show that oh the whole  thing is a parti